is the quotient-by-a-finite-flat-subgroup-scheme gate, and this file now
SHARES it with `exists_atkinLehner_x0` rather than duplicating it.

**(2) is PROVEN below**, and it is formal — BUT OVER `ℚ`, NOT OVER
`ℤ_(q)`; see the correction immediately below, which is the whole of the
2026-07-30 re-cut.  `hc.universal` descends `dd ↦ classify g (al.dual g dd)`
to a unique `w_{Y,ℚ} : Y ⟶ Y` over `ℚ`, and the SAME universal property
applied to the identity transformation, using `al.dual_dual`, forces
`w_{Y,ℚ} ≫ w_{Y,ℚ} = 𝟙 Y`.  This is the proof of `exists_atkinLehner_x0`'s
step 2 replayed verbatim, and it is carried out in
`exists_atkinLehnerModelAut_of_jNeronDatum` below.

**⚠ CORRECTION, 2026-07-30: THE DESCENT CANNOT BE PERFORMED OVER
`ℤ_(q)`, AND THE FIRST VERSION OF THIS CUT DID EXACTLY THAT.**  The
paragraph above used to say that `d.model.coarse.universal` descends the
moduli action over `Spec ℤ_(q)` — "nothing in it is specific to `ℚ`" —
and the release-17 merge RE-OPENED
`exists_atkinLehnerModelAut_of_jNeronDatum` because of it.  The reason is
a FAITHFULNESS repair upstream: `flt-lean-218` refuted
`exists_isNIsogenyPair` over a base of residue characteristic `p ∣ N`
