the genuine `w_N` rather than an arbitrary automorphism of `𝒴`, and
without it the whole conclusion is discharged by `w := 𝟙 𝒳`,
`w_𝒴 := 𝟙 𝒴`.

**WHERE THE HYPOTHESES ENTER.**  `q.Prime` with `q ≠ N` is INTENDED as `q ∤ N`,
i.e. good reduction: it is what lets the model be smooth at `q` at all, and
hence what makes `d` satisfiable.  It is carried explicitly as a guard
