/-- **A QUASI-FINITE MAP OF SMOOTH CURVES OVER A FIELD CARRIES GENERIC POINTS TO
GENERIC POINTS** (cut 2026-07-30 out of `flat_of_mono_of_curve_over_field` below;
**PROVEN 2026-07-31** — see the closing paragraphs).

This is the "one piece of real mathematics" that leaf's docstring identified,
stated in the exact contrapositive form its shortcut route consumes:
`ringKrullDim 𝒪_{X,x} = 0` says `x` is a maximal point of `X`, and the
conclusion says `u x` is a maximal point of `J`.

**THE CONTENT IS THE DIMENSION FORMULA FOR FINITE-TYPE `K`-SCHEMES**, and that
is the whole of it.  For `X` smooth of relative dimension `1` over `K` every
component has dimension `1`, so `ringKrullDim 𝒪_{X,x} = 0` forces
`trdeg_K κ(x) = 1`; `u` is unramified of finite type, hence quasi-finite, so
`κ(x) / κ(u x)` is FINITE and `trdeg_K κ(u x) = 1` as well; and on `J`, also
smooth of relative dimension `1`, that returns `ringKrullDim 𝒪_{J,u x} = 0`.
Neither `trdeg` nor the formula `dim 𝒪_{X,x} + trdeg_K κ(x) = dim X` is in the
pin as a statement about stalks, which is why this is a leaf and not a step.

**`hJsmooth` IS LOAD-BEARING and it is easy to think otherwise.**  Without it
`J` may have a component of dimension `> 1`, and a maximal point of `X` can then
map to a NON-maximal point of `J`: take `J` a smooth surface, `X` a smooth curve
inside it, `u` the closed immersion (a monomorphism, quasi-finite).  The generic
point of `X` is a codimension-`1` point of `J`, so `ringKrullDim 𝒪_{J,u x} = 1`.
So this leaf is genuinely about two curves, unlike its sibling above.

**WHY IT IS STATED WITH `Mono u` RATHER THAN `LocallyQuasiFinite u`.**  Only
quasi-finiteness is used, but `Mono` is what the consumer has, and deriving
`LocallyQuasiFinite` from it at the SCHEME level does not synthesize at this pin
(there is no `Unramified` morphism class — only `FormallyUnramified`, which
omits finite type).  The consumer below does not need the scheme-level property
at all: it goes through the STALK, where
`FormallyUnramified.stalkMap` and `LocallyOfFiniteType.stalkMap` give
`Algebra.FormallyUnramified` and `Algebra.EssFiniteType`, and mathlib's instance
turns that pair into `Algebra.QuasiFinite`.  A prover of this leaf can do the
same, or can restate it over `LocallyQuasiFinite u` and repair the one call site.

**THE CHECK THAT WOULD REFUTE IT**: a quasi-finite `K`-morphism between two
smooth `K`-curves carrying a maximal point to a non-maximal one.  By the above
that needs a component of `J` of dimension `≠ 1`, so a refutation is really a
refutation of "smooth of relative dimension `1` implies equidimensional of
dimension `1`".

**PROVEN 2026-07-31**, in
`Fermat/FLT/Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/CurveDimension.lean`, where it is stated
universe-polymorphically as
`AlgebraicGeometry.ringKrullDim_stalk_eq_zero_of_mono_of_curve_over_field`; this
declaration is that theorem at universe `0` and contains no mathematics.

The docstring above predicted the content correctly — it IS the dimension formula
— but overstated the cost, in one respect worth recording for the next reader.
**NO TRANSCENDENCE DEGREE HAD TO BE DEFINED.**  In relative dimension `1` both
sides of `dim 𝒪_{X,x} + trdeg_K κ(x) = dim X` are `0` or `1`, so the formula
degenerates to the DICHOTOMY "`dim 𝒪_{X,x} = 0` iff `κ(x)` is transcendental over
`K`", which is a statement about `Algebra.IsAlgebraic` alone.  That dichotomy is
proved in one affine chart from mathlib's local structure theorem
(`exists_etale_mvPolynomial`): `p` is minimal in the chart iff it contracts to `⊥`
in `K[X₁]` (quasi-finiteness one way, going-down the other), and contracting to `⊥`
is exactly transcendence of `κ(p)` (the variable, resp. the Nullstellensatz plus
finiteness of `κ(p)/κ(Q)`).

Two further things the docstring did not anticipate, and both were the actual work:

* the transfer along `u` is FREE.  Mathlib's
  `AlgebraicGeometry.FormallyUnramified` file carries an instance making
  `κ(x)` SEPARABLE over `κ(u x)` for `u` formally unramified and locally of finite
  type — so the "`κ(x)/κ(u x)` is finite" step is `inferInstance`, and the
  restatement over `LocallyQuasiFinite u` that this docstring offers as an option
  is not needed;
* what IS delicate is that the `K`-algebra structures on `κ(x)` and `κ(u x)` must
  be the CANONICAL ones (from `strX.residueFieldMap`, `jstr.residueFieldMap`), not
  the ones a chart supplies, or the two ends of `Algebra.IsAlgebraic.trans` carry
  unrelated `K`-structures.  Identifying the chart's structure with the canonical
  one is `Algebra.algebra_ext` plus `germ_res`; the scalar tower
  `K → κ(u x) → κ(x)` is where `hu` enters, via `Scheme.Γevaluation_naturality`. -/
theorem ringKrullDim_stalk_eq_zero_of_mono_of_curve_over_field
    {K : Type} [Field K] {X J : Scheme.{0}}
    {strX : X ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of K)} {jstr : J ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of K)}
    (hXsmooth : SmoothOfRelativeDimension 1 strX)
    (hJsmooth : SmoothOfRelativeDimension 1 jstr)
    (u : X ⟶ J) (hu : u ≫ jstr = strX) (hmono : Mono u) (x : X)
    (hx : ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk x) = 0) :
    ringKrullDim (J.presheaf.stalk (u.base x)) = 0 :=
  _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.ringKrullDim_stalk_eq_zero_of_mono_of_curve_over_field
    hXsmooth hJsmooth u hu hmono x hx

