`Fix(v)` is the equaliser `equalizer v (𝟙 d.E)` — a scheme, because `Scheme` has
all finite limits — and the claim is that it is finite over the base and reduced.
Everything else that leaf 2b used to carry (the arbitrary test scheme `W`, the
factorisation of `u` through `Fix(v)`, and the descent of the containment from
