of characteristic `0` — and its reducedness is then Cartier's theorem again,
which is **already proven and sorry-free in this tree**
(`CartierTheorem.isReduced_of_charZero`, `Fermat/FLT/GroupScheme/Cartier.lean`,
nameable here through `X0.lean`'s `public import`; the same route
`isReduced_cyc_of_algClosBase` above takes for `C`, via
`CyclicSubgroupOfOrder.exists_hopfAlgebra_geomFibre` and
`isReduced_geomFibre_of_specQBase`).  So: if the general `v` resists, ADD an
additivity hypothesis on `v` and discharge it at the call site from `hadd` —
`x ↦ Ψ x + Ψ x` is additive because `Ψ` is and the group law is commutative.
That trade is a strict improvement, since it replaces a missing theory by a
theorem already on disk.

*DONE 2026-07-30 (flt-lean-292): `_hadd` above IS that hypothesis, and it is
discharged at the only call site by `isAdditiveOn_twoPost` — which was written
