element of `RelPoint d.f d.f`, whose defining property IS `hv`.

**CHARACTERISTIC `0` IS LOAD-BEARING** here too — `Fix(Frobenius)` is not
reduced — which is again why the base is `Spec ℚ̄` and not a general
algebraically closed field.

**WHY THIS SHAPE RATHER THAN "`Fix(v)` IS A CLOSED SUBSCHEME CONTAINED IN `C`".**
The containment is NOT asked for here — it is derived below from these two
properties plus `hgeom`, by
`exists_factor_of_geomSections_of_isReduced_of_isFinite`, which needs no
separatedness of `d.E` and no ideal sheaf.  Asking for the containment directly
would have forced a prover to build the closed-immersion structure of the
