  `section_eq_of_range_eq_algClos` — PROVEN, and see the NAMEABILITY note below.

**THE GEOMETRY IS `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_unique_extension_of_isSmoothProperCurve`,
APPLIED TWICE.**  `d₁.E` and `d₂.E` are smooth proper geometrically connected
curves over `Spec ℚ̄` — `ab.proper`, `ab.connected` and
`Gamma0Datum.relativeDimensionOne`, field for field — and each chart's missing
locus is the range of a SECTION, hence one point, hence finite.  So `χ ≫ ι₂`
extends over `d₁.E` and `χ⁻¹ ≫ ι₁` over `d₂.E`; the two composites agree with
the identity on a dense open of a reduced separated scheme, so `u` is an
isomorphism.  `IsPullback d₁.f u (𝟙 _) d₂.f` is then
`IsPullback.of_vert_isIso`, both legs being isomorphisms.

**THE `ℚ̄` BASE MAKES THE ZERO-SECTION STEP EASIER, NOT HARDER**, which is the
one place this differs from the `ℚ`-side model
`Fermat.exists_geomFibreAddEquiv_of_weierstrassModel`.  There the step is
`hom_specRat_eq_of_range_eq`, a `ℚ`-only shortcut.  Here it is mathlib's
`AlgebraicGeometry.ext_of_apply_closedPoint_eq` (`AlgClosed/Basic.lean`), which
